  "job_B1.3.22_20251001_193206": {
    "text": "UI NONAS IULII, NATALE SANCTI SWY\u00f0UNI EPISCOPI.\nON EADGARES DAGUM \u00d0\u00c6S \u00c6\u00d0ELAN CYNINCGES, \u00deA\u00d0A se Cristendom w\u00e6s wel \u00f0eonde \u00feurh\nHis d\u00e6da n\u00e6ron cu\u00f0e \u00e6r\u00f0an \u00fee hi God sylf cydde, ne we ne fundon on bocum hu se bisceop leofode on\n\u00de\u00e6t w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6ra gymeleast \u00fee on life hine cu\u00feon, \u00fe\u00e6t hi noldon awritan his weorc and drohtnunge \u00feam\n\u00d0es Swy\u00f0un w\u00e6s bisceop on Winceastre, swa \u00feeah ofer Hamtunscire, ges\u00e6lig Godes \u00feeowa, and eahta\nNu n\u00e6s us his lif cu\u00f0 swa swa we \u00e6r cw\u00e6don, butan \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s bebyrged \u00e6t his bisceopstole be\n\u00derym gearum \u00e6r\u00f0an \u00fee se sanct into cyrcan w\u00e6re gebroht of \u00f0\u00e6re st\u00e6nenan \u00feryh \u00fee stent nu wi\u00f0innan\nSe smi\u00f0 \u00fea andwyrde \u00feam arwur\u00f0an Swy\u00f0une \u00feus, Gefyrn ic hine cu\u00f0e, leof, ac he ferde heonon and ic\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft se halga wer to \u00f0am ealdan smy\u00f0e, Witodlice he wuna\u00f0 nu on wincelcumbe hamf\u00e6st, and\nAnd se smi\u00f0 him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, La leof, Eadzige nele gelyfan minum wordum.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se bisceop eft, Gange him to minre byrgene, and ateo ane hringan up of \u00f0\u00e6re \u00feryh, and gif\nGif seo hringe nele up \u00feurh his anes tige \u00feonne ne sceall he nates hwon \u00feinre sage gelyfan.\nSege him eac si\u00f0\u00f0an, \u00fe\u00e6t he sylf gerihtl\u00e6ce his d\u00e6da and \u00feeawas to his drihtnes willan, and efste\nSege eac eallum mannum \u00fe\u00e6t sona swa hi geopenia\u00f0 mine byrgene, \u00fe\u00e6t hi magon \u00f0\u00e6r findan swa\nSe halga Swy\u00f0un \u00fea ferde fram \u00feam smi\u00f0 up, and se smi\u00f0e ne dorste secgan \u00feas gesih\u00f0e \u00e6nigum menn,\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a se halga wer hine eft gespr\u00e6c and git \u00feryddan si\u00f0e, and swy\u00f0e hine \u00fereade, hwi he nolde\nSe smi\u00f0 \u00fea \u00e6t nextan eode swa \u00f0eah to his byrgene, and genam ane hringan earhlice swa \u00f0eah, and\nHe teah \u00f0a \u00fe\u00e6t isen up swa ea\u00f0elice up of \u00f0am stane swilce hit on sande stode, and he swy\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6s\nHe \u00f0a hit eft sette on \u00fe\u00e6t ylce \u00feyrl, and \u00feyde mid his fet, and hit swa f\u00e6ste eft stod \u00fe\u00e6t nan man ne\n\u00dea eode se smi\u00f0 geegsod \u00feanon, and gemette on cypincge \u00fe\u00e6s Eadzies mann, and s\u00e6de him gewislice\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he hit wolde cy\u00f0an his hlaforde, and ne dorste swa \u00f0eah hit secgan \u00e6t fruman, \u00e6r\u00fean \u00f0e\n\u00dea onscunode se Eadsige A\u00f0elwold \u00feone bisceop and ealle \u00f0a munecas \u00fee on \u00f0am mynstre w\u00e6ron, for\nHe gebeah swa \u00feeah binnan twam gearum to \u00feam ylcan mynstre and munuc wear\u00f0 \u00feurh God, and \u00fe\u00e6r\nGebl\u00e6tsod is se ealmihtiga God \u00fee geeadmed \u00feone modigan, and \u00f0a eadmodan ah\u00e6f\u00f0 to healicum\nEft w\u00e6s sum earm ceorl egeslicc gehoferod, and \u00f0earle gebiged \u00feurh \u00f0one bradan hofor.\n\u00deam wear\u00f0 geswutelod on swefne gewislice, \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde gefeccan \u00e6t Swy\u00f0unes byrgene his\nHe aras \u00f0a on mergen micclum f\u00e6gnigende, and mid twam criccum creap him to Wynceastre, and\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea geh\u00e6led \u00feurh \u00feone halgan bisceop, swa \u00fe\u00e6t n\u00e6s gesyne sy\u00f0\u00f0an on his hricge hw\u00e6r se\n\u00dea nyston \u00fea munecas be \u00f0am m\u00e6ran halgan, and wendon \u00fe\u00e6t sum o\u00f0er halga geh\u00e6lde \u00feone mann, ac\nSum wer w\u00e6s geuntrumod swi\u00f0e yfelum broce, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he earfo\u00f0lice \u00fea eagan undyde, and unea\u00f0e\n\u00d0a woldon his freond ealle hine ferian to niwan mynstre to \u00feam halgan Iudoce, \u00fe\u00e6t he him h\u00e6le\nHi wacodon \u00f0a \u00fea niht wi\u00f0 \u00fea byrgene mid him, biddende \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan God, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0am adligan\nSe untruma eac wacode o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t hit wolde dagian, \u00fea wear\u00f0 he on sl\u00e6pe and seo wur\u00f0fulle byrgen \u00fe\u00e6s\nHe w\u00e6s \u00f0a geh\u00e6led \u00feurh \u00f0one halgan Swy\u00f0un, and man sohte \u00feone sco swy\u00f0e geornlice, ac hine ne\nAnd hi gewendan \u00fea ham mid \u00feam geh\u00e6ledan menn.\n\u00de\u00e6r wurdon geh\u00e6lede \u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6re halgan byrgene eahta untrume menn, \u00e6r\u00f0an \u00fee he of \u00f0\u00e6re byrgene up\nEadgar cyning \u00fea \u00e6fter \u00f0ysum tacnum wolde \u00fe\u00e6t se halga wer wurde up gedon, and spr\u00e6c hit to\n\u00dea se bisceop A\u00f0elwold mid abbodum and munecum, dyde up \u00feone sanct mid sange wur\u00f0lice, and\n\u00de\u00e6r he stend mid wur\u00f0mynte and wundra gefrema\u00f0.\n\u00de\u00e6r wurdon geh\u00e6lede \u00feurh \u00f0one halgan wer feower wanhale menn binnan \u00f0rym dagum, and geond fif\nBinnon tyn dagum \u00fe\u00e6r wurdon twa hund manna geh\u00e6lede, and swa fela binnan twelf mon\u00f0um \u00fe\u00e6t\nSe lictun l\u00e6g afylled mid alefedum mannum, swa \u00fe\u00e6t man ea\u00f0e ne mihte \u00fe\u00e6t mynster gesecan; and \u00fea\nOn \u00feam dagum w\u00e6ron on Wihtlande \u00fereo wif, \u00fea twa w\u00e6ron blinde geond nigon geara fec, and \u00fe\u00e6t\nHi begeaton \u00fea earfo\u00f0lice him \u00e6nne latteow \u00e6nne dumbne cnapan and comon to \u00feam halgan, and ane\n\u00dea s\u00e6de se cnapa \u00feam cyrcwerde \u00fe\u00e6t, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6fre \u00e6r naht cwe\u00f0an ne mihte, and b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re ylcan tide w\u00e6s sum wyln geh\u00e6ft to swinglum for swy\u00f0e lytlan gylte, and l\u00e6g on h\u00e6ftnedum\n\u00dea wacode heo ealle \u00f0a niht and mid wope clypode to \u00f0am halgan Swy\u00f0une \u00fe\u00e6t he hulpe hire earmre,\nMid \u00feam \u00fee hit dagode and man drihtnes lofsang ongan, \u00fea feollan \u00f0a fotcopsas f\u00e6rlice hire fram, and\nSum \u00feegn l\u00e6g alefed lange on paralisyn, and ne mihte of his bedde for manegum gearum.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde to wynceastre sy\u00f0ian huru on his horsb\u00e6re, and biddan his h\u00e6le.\nMid \u00feam \u00fee he \u00feis cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his cnihtum and freondum, \u00fea wear\u00f0 he geh\u00e6led, and gewende swa \u00feeah\nFif and twentig manna myslice geuntrume comon to \u00feam halgan heora h\u00e6le biddende; sume w\u00e6ron\nSum \u00feegn w\u00e6s on Engla lande on \u00e6htum swy\u00f0e welig, se wear\u00f0 f\u00e6rlice blind, \u00fea ferde he to Rome,\nHe wunode \u00fea on Rome and ne wear\u00f0 geh\u00e6led feower gear fullice; and befran \u00fea be Swy\u00f0une, hwylce\nSum wer w\u00e6s eac blind wel seofon gear fulle, se h\u00e6fde \u00e6nne latteow \u00fee hine l\u00e6dde gehwider.\n\u00d0a sume d\u00e6g eode he swa swa he oft dyde, and se latteow wear\u00f0 gebolgen and \u00feone blindan forlet,\nGemiltsa me, Drihten, \u00feurh \u00f0one m\u00e6ran Swy\u00f0un, and forgif me gesih\u00f0e, for \u00f0\u00e6s sanctes\nEft he clypode \u00feus, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00f0am halgan, Eala \u00feu milda bisceop \u00fee manega wundra of cuma\u00f0 \u00feurh\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea geh\u00e6led, and h\u00e6fde his gesih\u00f0e, and ham eode bly\u00f0e butan latteowe ana, se \u00f0e lytle \u00e6r\nA\u00feelwold \u00fea se arwur\u00f0a and se eadiga bisceop, \u00fee on \u00f0am dagum w\u00e6s on Winceastre bisceop, bead\n\u00dea dydon hi sona swa, and sungon \u00feone lofsang, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t heom la\u00f0ode eallum \u00fe\u00e6t hi swa oft arisan,\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a se halga Swy\u00f0un sylf com on swefne wundorlice geglencged to sumum godan menn and\n\u00dea aw\u00e6cnode se wer of \u00feam wynsuman sl\u00e6pe, and swy\u00f0e besargode \u00fe\u00e6t he geseon ne moste ne nan\nHe aras swa\u00f0eah and swi\u00f0e hra\u00f0e ferde to A\u00feelwolde bisceope, and him eall \u00feis s\u00e6de.\nA\u00feelwold \u00fea asende sona to \u00feam munecum of cyninges hyrede, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t hi sceoldon \u00feone\nHi hit heoldon \u00fea sy\u00f0\u00f0an symle on gewunon, swa swa we gesawon sylfe for oft, and \u00feone sang we\nSum wer w\u00e6s betogen \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6re on stale, w\u00e6s swa\u00f0eah unscyldig, and hine man sona gel\u00e6hte and\n\u00dea w\u00e6s he seofon mon\u00f0as wunigende swa blind, and his hlyst n\u00e6fde, o\u00fe\u00fe\u00e6t he mid geleafan ferde to\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 Godes wundor geworht an \u00feam menn \u00feurh Swy\u00f0unes \u00feingunge \u00fe\u00e6t he geseah beorhte\nHim w\u00e6s eac forgifen \u00fe\u00e6t he wel mihte gehyran, se \u00f0e \u00e6r n\u00e6fde ne eagan ne hlyst.\nIs swa \u00f0eah to witenne \u00fe\u00e6t we ne moton us gebiddan, swa to Godes halgum swa swa to Gode sylfum,\nHwilon wacodon menn swa swa hit gewunelic is ofer an dead lic, and \u00f0\u00e6r w\u00e6s sum dysig mann\nGe magon to so\u00f0um witan \u00fe\u00e6t ic Swy\u00f0un eom se \u00f0e wundra wyrc\u00f0, and ic wille \u00fe\u00e6t ge beran eower\nHe woffode \u00f0a swa lange mid wordum dyslice, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t he feoll geswogen swylce he sawlleas w\u00e6re,\nHis magas \u00f0a \u00e6t nextan \u00feone mann feredon to \u00feam halgan Swi\u00feune, and he sylf andette his dyslican\nIs eac to witenne \u00fe\u00e6t menn unwislice do\u00f0 \u00fea \u00f0e dwollice plega\u00f0 \u00e6t deadra manna lice, and \u00e6lce\nSume menn eac drinca\u00f0 \u00e6t deadra manna lice ofer ealle \u00fea niht swi\u00f0e unrihtlice, and gremia\u00f0 God\nHwilon comon to \u00f0am halgan hundtwelftig manna mislice geuntrumode mid manegum brocum, and\nSumes \u00feegnes cniht feoll f\u00e6rlice of his horse \u00fe\u00e6t him tob\u00e6rst se earm and se o\u00f0er sceanca, and swi\u00f0e\nHe w\u00e6s his hlaforde swy\u00fee leof \u00e6r\u00fean, and se hlaford \u00fea besargode swy\u00f0e \u00feone cniht, and b\u00e6d \u00feone\nHe clypode eac to Swi\u00f0une \u00feus secgende mid geomerunge, Eala \u00f0u halga Swi\u00f0un, bide \u00feone H\u00e6lend\nSe cniht \u00f0a aras hal geh\u00e6led \u00feurh sancte Swi\u00feun, and se hlaford \u00fe\u00e6s f\u00e6gnode, and mid geleafan God\nSum eald \u00feegn w\u00e6s eac on Wihtlande untrum, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he l\u00e6g b\u00e6ddryda sume nigon gear, and of \u00f0am\nHim comon \u00fea on swefne to twegen scinende halgan, and heton hine yrnan ardlice mid him, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don \u00fea halgan, \u00feu cymst to \u00f0\u00e6re stowe gif \u00f0u f\u00e6rst mid us nu, \u00f0\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r \u00f0u underfehst \u00feine\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea swy\u00f0e f\u00e6gen, and wolde faran mid heom, ac \u00fea\u00fea he ne mihte heom mid sy\u00f0ian, \u00fea\nAnd se halga Swi\u00f0un on scinendum m\u00e6ssereafe stod \u00e6t \u00f0am weofode, swylce he wolde m\u00e6ssian.\nSwy\u00f0un cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea sona to \u00feam seocan menn, ic secge \u00f0e bro\u00f0or, \u00feu ne scealt heononfor\u00f0 nanon menn\nSe adliga \u00fea \u00f0ohte \u00fe\u00e6t he yfel nolde don buton \u00feam anum \u00fee him \u00e6r yfel dyde, and \u00f0am wolde don\n\u00dea wiste se halga Swi\u00f0un hu his heorte smeade, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 bli\u00f0elice him to, Bro\u00f0or, ic \u00fee secge, ne do\nEac cw\u00e6\u00f0 Paulus se apostol to eallum Cristenum mannum, gif \u00f0inum fynd hingrige fed hine mid\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se bedryda to \u00f0am bisceope eft, La leof, sege me hw\u00e6t \u00feu sy manna, nu \u00f0u manna heortan\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se halga Swy\u00f0un, ic eom se\u00fee nu niwan com, swylce he cw\u00e6de swa, ic w\u00e6s geswutelod nu\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se b\u00e6dryda to \u00f0am bisceope eft, hu eart \u00f0u gehaten?\nAnd se halga him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, \u00feonne \u00f0u cymst to Winceastre, \u00feu wast minne naman.\nSe man wear\u00f0 \u00fea gebroht to his bedde eft sona, and awoc of sl\u00e6pe, and s\u00e6de his wife ealle \u00f0a gesih\u00f0e\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t wif him to \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6re Swy\u00f0un se \u00f0e hine l\u00e6rde mid \u00fe\u00e6re halgan lare and \u00feone \u00f0e he\nHeo cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0a to \u00feam were, hit w\u00e6re nu full good \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0e man b\u00e6re to cyrcan, and \u00feu b\u00e6de \u00feone\nHine man b\u00e6r \u00f0a sona of \u00f0am bedde to cyrcan binnan Withlande, and he wear\u00f0 geh\u00e6led sona \u00feurh\nHe ferde eac si\u00f0\u00f0an to winceastre forra\u00f0e, and cydde A\u00f0elwolde \u00feam arwur\u00fean bisceope, hu he wear\u00f0\nNu is to witenne \u00fe\u00e6t we ne sceolan cepan ealles to swy\u00f0e be swefnum, for\u00f0an \u00fee hi ealle ne beo\u00f0 of\nSume swefna syndon so\u00f0lice of Gode, swa swa we on bocum r\u00e6da\u00f0, and sume beo\u00f0 of deofle to\n\u00dea swefna beo\u00f0 wynsume \u00fee gewur\u00f0a\u00fe of Gode, and \u00fea beo\u00f0 egefulle \u00f0e of \u00feam deofle cuma\u00f0, and\nSum man on Winceastre wear\u00f0 yrre his \u00f0eowan men for sumere gymeleaste, and gesette hine on\nHe s\u00e6t \u00f0a swa lange on \u00feam la\u00f0um bendum, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t he best\u00e6l ut mid his stafe hoppende, and gesohte\nSe scyttel \u00f0a asceat sona of \u00fe\u00e6re fetere, and se \u00f0eowa aras ahred \u00feurh \u00f0one halgan.\nSum mann w\u00e6s gebunden onbutan \u00fe\u00e6t heafod for his hefigum gylte, se com to \u00feam halgan, and his\nNe mage we awritan ne mid wordum asecgan ealle \u00fea wundra \u00fee se halga wer Swi\u00f0un, \u00feurh God\nSeo ealde cyrce w\u00e6s eall behangen mid criccum, and mid creopera sceamelum, fram ende o\u00f0 o\u00feerne\n\u00deyllice tacna cy\u00fea\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t Crist is \u00e6lmihtig God, \u00fee his halgan geswutelode \u00feurh swylce weld\u00e6da, \u00feeah\n\u00deonne buga\u00f0 \u00fea earmingas on ende \u00feysre worulde \u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6r to lafe beo\u00f0 mid geleafan to Criste, and \u00f0a\nWe habba\u00f0 nu ges\u00e6d be Swi\u00f0une \u00feus sceortlice, and we secga\u00f0 to so\u00f0an \u00fe\u00e6t se tima w\u00e6s ges\u00e6lig and\n\u00de\u00e6rtoeacan w\u00e6ron swilce wundra gefremode \u00feurh \u00feone halgan Swy\u00f0un, swa swa we s\u00e6don \u00e6r, and\nOn \u00f0am timan w\u00e6ron eac wur\u00f0fulle bisceopas, Dunstan se anr\u00e6da \u00e6t \u00f0am ercestole, and A\u00feelwold se\nITEM ALIA.\nMannum is eac to witenne \u00fe\u00e6t manega drymen macia\u00f0 menigfealde dydrunga \u00feurh deofles cr\u00e6ft, swa\nBe \u00f0am we magan secgan sume so\u00f0e bysne.\nMacharius w\u00e6s gehaten sum halig f\u00e6der on w\u00e6stene wunigende, fela wundra wyrcende munuclifes\n\u00de\u00e6t m\u00e6den w\u00e6s swa forbroden swylce heo an myre w\u00e6re, and eallum \u00feam \u00feuhte \u00fee hire onlocodon\n\u00dea leddon hire magas hi to Macharie, and he sona axode hw\u00e6t hi woldon mid \u00feam.\n\u00dea magas him cw\u00e6don to, \u00feeos myre \u00fee \u00f0u gesihst w\u00e6s ure dohtor arwur\u00f0e m\u00e6den; ac awyrigde\nNu bidde we \u00f0e, leof, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u gebide for hi and hi eft awende to \u00feam \u00f0e heo \u00e6r w\u00e6s.\nMacharius \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 to hire magum \u00f0us, Ic geseo \u00feis m\u00e6den on menniscum gecynde, and heo nis na\nMacharius \u00f0a geb\u00e6d for \u00fe\u00e6t m\u00e6den God, and mid ele gesmyrode, and mid ealle adr\u00e6fde \u00feas deofles\nSwylce synd \u00fea dydrunga \u00fe\u00e6re drymanna.\nSy wuldor and lof \u00feam welwillendan scyppende \u00fee his halgan m\u00e6rsa\u00f0 mihtiglice mid wundrum, se\u00f0e",
